   "tipo": "explicacion",
   "titulo": "The verbs in -er",
   "texto": [
    "Most French verbs end up in **-er**. Regular ones, such as **parler** (talk), **habiter** (live) and **travailler** (work), follow the same model; **aller** (go) is a frequent irregular exception.",
    "In the regular verbs, **-er** is removed and the endings are added: **-e, -es, -e, -ons, -ez, -ent**.",
    "The important thing when speaking: **je parle, tu parles, il parle** and **ils parlent** sound **exactamente igual** («parl»). Only different **nous parlons** and **vous parlez** are heard."
   ]
  },
